From b8b992390ed8e10b21e2014a1625799f734c5c04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:15:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-95: reparent on the design surface (Alt at the
 release), like Blend; into the form = the form itself (0.95.0)

Blend (Artboard modifier keys): "Reparent an object: drag the object over a
layout panel and press Alt before releasing the mouse button". Here a drag on
the surface only moved; changing the container needed the component tree.
Now a move let go with Alt held puts the originals back and posts
reparentDrop (where each one's top-left is from the pointer, and the id'd
elements under the pointer -- the dragged ones hidden while looking -- each
with the pointer in its own coordinates). cmdReparentDrop takes the first
container (Panel / GroupBox / the form; a tab sheet is refused and said):
the one they are in = just that move (a batch setLayout); another one =
cmdReparent with the drop place (pos: each unit's first tag moved to it), one
undo.

Fix found by the real VS Code test: htmlblock.insideEnd took the first
<div class="cli"> ANYWHERE inside the container, so a paste / a toolbox add /
an outline drop / this reparent "into the form" landed in the form's first
GroupBox. Now only a direct child cli counts.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 160, smoke 186, panels, real VS Code 159): lib
(into the form with a GroupBox inside = the form's own end); probe (let go
with Alt over a box of its own: reparentDrop with the name, -5 / -5 from the
pointer, the box then the form; the button back, nothing written); smoke (into
the form at 295, 244, not in Panel2 nor GroupBox1; over its own Panel2 just
the move; over no container nothing); real VS Code (into the form, the tree
says so, one undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
